<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Truce of Deulino</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1618</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-muscovite-war-1605-1618">Polish–Muscovite War (1605–1618)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Truce of Deulino was an armistice concluded in 1618 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> and Muscovy, ending a period of war during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/time-of-troubles">Time of Troubles</a>. It confirmed Polish-Lithuanian possession of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smolensk">Smolensk</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chernigov">Chernigov</a>. The Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth profile describes it as representing the maximum territorial achievement of Commonwealth arms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/truce-of-deulino.jpg" alt="Truce of Deulino" width="320" height="251" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Mathiasrex Maciej Szczepańczyk, based on layers of User:Halibutt · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Truce_of_Deulino_1618-1619.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
